;
; One load, nothing else in the way.
;
; The ELF loader now says where a load spends its time (patch 0039): bytes
; read and milliseconds reading, against sections relocated and milliseconds
; relocating, printed once per load and only when the load took over a second.
;
; ISSUE-0051 established that the I/O cannot account for the failure -- 20 MB
; read at the rate this card gives is about twelve seconds, against an open
; that does not return in four hundred. This is the measurement that says what
; the rest of it is.
;
; Nothing is opened before the big one, so the line that comes out belongs to
; mesa3dgl20-0.library and to nothing else.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[gl-load] --- OpenMesa mesa3dgl20-0.library (10 MB)"
Date >DEBUG:
OpenMesa mesa3dgl20-0.library >NIL: <NIL:
Date >DEBUG:
Echo >DEBUG: "[gl-load] --- returned"
